# Documentation / Non-Runtime Content
# FLT-IGN-1 (2026.09.27): this block was a blanket `*.md` with two negations. It
# ignored every markdown file in the repo except README.md and mForceOS1.md — so
# the app's own mForceLibrary.md, mForceVision.md and projectConfig.md reported a
# clean tree when edited and were silently lost on the next clone.
# Commit 14ff150 ("Cleanup: apply tight gitignore and remove non-runtime files")
# shows what the rule was actually aimed at: 69 bulk content-site markdown files,
# every one of them under docs/ or legacy_content/docs/. Those trees have since
# been moved under _archive/ (ignored on its own below), so the blanket pattern was
# protecting nothing that another rule did not already cover.
# Narrowed to the two original paths, anchored to the repo root so a nested docs/
# directory inside the app is not caught. App-level markdown is tracked again.
/docs/
/legacy_content/

# archived one-time/non-runtime files (local only)
_archive/

# fleet tooling (local)
mForce.sh

