# Angular build cache — local only, regenerated on every build (2026.09.16).
# It appeared untracked after a local `npm test` run and `git add -A` in the bake
# would have committed it.
**/.angular/

# ── gcloud config dir: spelling gap found 2026.09.27 alongside FLT-IGN-1 ──
# The fleet-standard block above guards `.gcloud_config/` with an UNDERSCORE, but the
# directory in this repo is `.gcloud-config/` with a HYPHEN, so the guard never
# matched and 8 files under mForceLibrary_v1.0.0/.gcloud-config/ are already tracked,
# including access_tokens.db and credentials.db. This line stops any further files
# being added, but .gitignore does not untrack what is already in the index:
# those two credential stores are still in the repo and in its history.
# ACTION REQUIRED (needs a write command, deliberately not run here):
#   git rm -r --cached mForceLibrary_v1.0.0/.gcloud-config
# and treat the gcloud credentials as exposed — revoke/rotate them.
.gcloud-config/
**/.gcloud-config/

# ── fluxive cleanup guard · managed, 2026.09.30 ──────────────────────────
# Added after a fleet audit found 5 GB of build output, virtualenvs, logs and
# editor backups on disk — 332 MB of it committed. These are the shapes that
# kept coming back. A .gitignore does not untrack what is already tracked; it
# stops the next copy arriving.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
venv/
*venv/
.venv/
site-packages/
node_modules/
build/
dist/
webapp-dist/
desktop_package/
canvaskit/
flutter_assets/
main.dart.js
*.min.js
*.bundle.js
flutter_service_worker.js
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.orig
*.rej
*.pre_*
*.stale_*
# ── end fluxive cleanup guard ───────────────────────────────────────────
